ive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": ["scintillate"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(intransitive, of a gun) To shoot; to fire", "tags": ["intransitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "[Streetlife]:Fuck a peace talk, let the gun spark, on the streets of New York.", "reference": "1998 November 10, “Grid Iron Rap” (track 17), in Tical 2000: Judgement Day, performed by Method Man, Streetlife (rapper):"}, {"text": "All of a sudden, everybody tuggin', everybody dark. Everybody gums runnin', 'til the guns spark.", "reference": "2004, “U Ain't A Killer” (track 10), in The War Mixtape, performed by Akala (rapper):"}, {"text": "Guns spark in the dark, it was all just a part of the eighties Bronx scene that created all.", "reference": "2022 February 22, “Raw Hip Hop” (track 2), in IMAMCRU12, performed by KRS-One:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/spɑɹk/", "tags": ["General American"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/spɑːk/", "tags": ["Received Pronunciation"]}], "forms": [{"word": "sparks", "tags": ["plural"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "A gallant; a foppish young man.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The finest sparks and cleanest beaux.", "reference": "1718, Mat[thew] Prior, “Alma: Or, The Progress of the Mind”, in Poems on Several Occasions, London: […] Jacob Tonson […], and John Barber […], →OCLC:"}, {"text": "Jones had no sooner quitted the room, than the petty-fogger, in a whispering tone, asked Mrs Whitefield, “If she knew who that fine spark was?”", "reference": "1749, Henry Fielding, The History of Tom Jones, a Foundling, volume (please specify |volume=I to VI), London: A[ndrew] Millar, […], →OCLC:"}, {"text": "He will retrieve his errors yet—their worthy Father, once my honour'd master, was at his years nea